IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`

-- coa19-nouns.l4: helpers shared by the coa19 modules (Part 25, Company charges, ss 859A to 894).
-- No section of the Act is "implemented" here except as noted: a three-valued AND and OR over MAYBE BOOLEAN answers, the one
-- way the Act counts 21 days ("21 days beginning with the day after the day on which ..."), and the pounds a fine limit
-- stands for. Every name begins with a section label (the keel's naming rule); the helpers are labelled with the first
-- section that needs them and are NOT a restatement of that section.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER IN THE coa19 MODULES (the rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled by a lawyer; see NOTES.md).
--   JUST TRUE   the text says the case is within the rule.
--   JUST FALSE  the text says no in its own words ("means", "if", "only if", "where", "when", "does not apply", "shall not").
--               Each such branch carries a comment  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "<quoted words>"
--   NOTHING     the text does not decide (silent, list not closed, includes, undefined term, points outside the text,
--               limited by its own wording). Each such branch carries a comment  -- NOTHING-kind (<why>)
--   A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.

-- Three-valued AND over two MAYBE BOOLEAN answers: JUST FALSE if either is JUST FALSE; JUST TRUE if both are; else NOTHING.
GIVEN first IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      second IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 859A both answers hold` MEANS
    CONSIDER first
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN second
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        CONSIDER second
        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- Three-valued OR: JUST TRUE if either is JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE if both are JUST FALSE; else NOTHING.
GIVEN first IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      second IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 859A either answer holds` MEANS
    CONSIDER first
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN second
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        CONSIDER second
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- A MAYBE BOOLEAN answer is "JUST TRUE" (a helper for conditions that need the answer to hold, not merely not fail).
GIVEN answer IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 859A the answer is JUST TRUE` MEANS answer EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- The Act counts a period "21 days beginning with the day after the day on which X": day 1 is the day after X, so the
-- last day is X plus 21 days. (The same counting in ss 859A(4), 859B(6), 870 and 886.)
-- src:11604 | (4) “The period allowed for delivery” is 21 days beginning with the day after the date of creation of the charge (see section 859E), unless an order allowing an extended period is made under section 859F(3).
@ref s 859A(4) The period allowed for delivery (src:11604-11604)
GIVEN `the day the period counts from` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 859A(4) the last day of 21 days beginning with the day after` MEANS
    Date (Day `the day the period counts from` PLUS 21)

-- "within 7 days of the order or of the appointment": the day of the order is not counted, so the last day is that day
-- plus 7 days (ss 859K(2), 868(3)(b), 871(1)).
-- src:11737 | (2) The person must, within 7 days of the order or of the appointment under those powers—
@ref s 859K(2) within 7 days of the order or of the appointment (src:11737-11737)
GIVEN `the day the period counts from` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 859K(2) the last day of 7 days after` MEANS
    Date (Day `the day the period counts from` PLUS 7)

-- The pounds that a limit on a fine stands for. A level on the standard scale and the statutory maximum are set outside the
-- Act, so the pounds are INPUTS (never guessed). Only level 3 and the statutory maximum occur in ss 859A to 894.
-- src:11755 | (7) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 859K(7) fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale, daily default fine one-tenth of level 3 (src:11755-11755)
GIVEN limit IS A `Fine limit`
      `the pounds that level 3 on the standard scale stands for` IS A NUMBER
      `the pounds that the statutory maximum stands for` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 859K(7) the most in pounds that the fine limit allows` MEANS
    CONSIDER limit
    WHEN `a fine without a stated limit` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text sets no limit ("to a fine")
    WHEN `a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` fraction THEN JUST (fraction TIMES `the pounds that the statutory maximum stands for`)
    WHEN `a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` level fraction THEN
        IF level EQUALS 3
        THEN JUST (fraction TIMES `the pounds that level 3 on the standard scale stands for`)
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): only level 3 occurs in ss 859A to 894
    WHEN `a fine not exceeding an amount in pounds` pounds THEN JUST pounds

-- Whether a thing that had to be done before the end of a period was done in time. The day it was done is a MAYBE DATE (NOTHING if it
-- has not been done); the day the question is asked says whether the period has run out. JUST TRUE: done on or before the last day.
-- JUST FALSE: done after the last day, or not done and the last day has passed (the text fixes the period in its own words, so outside
-- it the answer is JUST FALSE: the 2026-11-05 ruling on periods). NOTHING: not yet done and the period is still open.
-- Used by every "before the end of the period" and "within 7 days" duty of ss 859H, 859K, 860, 862, 871, 878 and 880.
-- src:11704 | (b) the documents required by section 859A or (as the case may be) 859B are not delivered to the registrar by the company or another person interested in the charge before the end of the relevant period allowed for delivery.
@ref s 859H(1)(b) not delivered before the end of the relevant period allowed for delivery (src:11704-11704)
GIVEN `the day it was done` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the last day of the period` IS A DATE
      `the day the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 859H(1)(b) the thing was done by the last day of the period` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day it was done`
    WHEN JUST done THEN
        IF done AT MOST `the last day of the period`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "before the end of the relevant period allowed for delivery": done after the last day
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        IF `the day the question is asked` AT MOST `the last day of the period`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): not yet done, and the period has not yet run out
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "before the end of the relevant period allowed for delivery": not done and the last day has passed
